WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.620 --> 00:00:02.520
Looking to Netflix and chill this weekend?

00:00:02.520 --> 00:00:03.540
We've got just the thing.

00:00:03.800 --> 00:00:07.580
Catch all these killer films before they leave
the streaming platform possibly for good.

00:00:07.680 --> 00:00:11.520
Each of these titles will be gone by September
1st, so time is of the essence here.

00:00:11.720 --> 00:00:12.220
Godspeed!

00:00:13.240 --> 00:00:17.360
The Hangover redefined the comedy genre when
it stormed into theaters in 2009.

00:00:17.580 --> 00:00:22.380
Starring Bradley Cooper, Ed Helms, Doug Billings,
and Zach Galifianakis, the film follows four

00:00:22.550 --> 00:00:26.920
theoretically upstanding young men as they
descend upon Las Vegas for a bachelor party.

00:00:26.930 --> 00:00:30.940
But the night they arrive, these standup dudes
get fall-down drunk... and wake up the next

00:00:30.940 --> 00:00:33.280
morning with no recollection of the night
before.

00:00:33.440 --> 00:00:35.840
What's worse, the groom-to-be has mysteriously
gone missing.

00:00:36.320 --> 00:00:37.320
"I looked everywhere.

00:00:37.800 --> 00:00:40.280
Gym, casino, the front desk — nobody has
seen Doug.

00:00:40.280 --> 00:00:40.780
He's not here."

00:00:41.280 --> 00:00:45.199
Now, it's a race against time as everyone
scrambles to retrace their steps and find

00:00:45.200 --> 00:00:47.720
Doug before his fiancée figures out what's
going on.

00:00:48.020 --> 00:00:49.020
"Where's Doug?"

00:00:49.140 --> 00:00:51.140
"He is… paying the bill.

00:00:51.160 --> 00:00:54.900
We just had a delicious brunch and we're in
a big hurry to get back so we gotta be going!"

00:00:55.320 --> 00:00:58.900
Throughout their quest, they encounter some
intensely strange and unsavory characters,

00:00:59.040 --> 00:01:01.540
all while suffering from the mother of all
hangovers.

00:01:05.170 --> 00:01:08.020
The Hangover will be staggering away from
Netflix on September 1st.

00:01:09.020 --> 00:01:13.040
It's the film that reinvigorated the Batman
property after the critical and commercial

00:01:13.040 --> 00:01:15.660
failure of 1997's Batman and Robin.

00:01:15.860 --> 00:01:21.710
Released in 2005, Batman Begins stars Christain
Bale as Bruce Wayne, a dark and brooding gentleman

00:01:21.710 --> 00:01:24.360
who witnessed the brutal murder of his parents
as a child.

00:01:24.590 --> 00:01:28.900
Wayne eventually becomes a full-fledged vigilante,
determined to wipe crime off the streets of

00:01:28.900 --> 00:01:29.780
Gotham City.

00:01:29.930 --> 00:01:34.700
Operating under the guise of Batman, the caped
crusader battles the nefarious psychiatrist

00:01:34.700 --> 00:01:37.200
Dr. Jonathan Crane, portrayed by Cillian Murphy.

00:01:37.800 --> 00:01:39.420
"Psychopharmacology is my …”

00:01:45.180 --> 00:01:47.040
“In here only the mind can grant you power."

00:01:47.520 --> 00:01:51.610
Otherwise known as Scarecrow, this iconic
baddie is hellbent on plunging the city into

00:01:51.610 --> 00:01:52.720
the depths of chaos.

00:01:52.880 --> 00:01:54.340
The question is: Will he succeed?

00:01:54.540 --> 00:01:58.440
Find out before Batman Begins flies away from
Netflix on September 1st.

00:01:59.060 --> 00:02:03.120
Hey, here's an idea: Why not turn your evening
into a dark and disturbing double feature?

00:02:03.120 --> 00:02:07.320
You simply can't go wrong with The Dark Knight,
the 2008 sequel to Batman Begins.

00:02:07.460 --> 00:02:11.940
This time, Batman takes on one of his most
notorious rivals: The Joker, played to perfection

00:02:11.940 --> 00:02:13.200
by the late Heath Ledger.

00:02:13.680 --> 00:02:16.240
"Why so serious?"

00:02:17.400 --> 00:02:21.599
Throughout the film, the maniacal madman commits
countless crimes, undercutting Batman's status

00:02:21.600 --> 00:02:25.140
in Gotham and plunging the city into complete
and utter darkness.

00:02:25.240 --> 00:02:28.540
This time, the question is: Has Batman finally
met his match?

00:02:28.600 --> 00:02:32.020
It's the perfect time to reacquaint yourself
with Ledger's iconic performance.

00:02:32.340 --> 00:02:36.100
On October 4th, Todd Phillips' Joker film
will give us a freaky new spin on the Clown

00:02:36.100 --> 00:02:40.000
Prince of Crime, portrayed by the always captivating
Joaquin Phoenix.

00:02:40.440 --> 00:02:42.940
“Haha.”

00:02:45.320 --> 00:02:48.440
The Dark Knight will be zipping away from
Netflix on September 1st.

00:02:49.140 --> 00:02:53.180
Sweeney Todd: The Demon Barber of Fleet Street
is probably one of Tim Burton's weirdest and

00:02:53.189 --> 00:02:57.340
most wonderful movies and that's saying a
lot considering all the outlandish oddities

00:02:57.340 --> 00:02:58.340
he's made in the past.

00:02:58.340 --> 00:03:03.250
A silver screen translation of Stephen Sondheim
and Hugh Wheeler's musical of the same name,

00:03:03.250 --> 00:03:08.010
Sweeney Todd features Johnny Depp in the title
role, a barber-slash-serial killer who cuts

00:03:08.010 --> 00:03:11.260
the hair and throats of his customers with
his signature straight razor.

00:03:11.600 --> 00:03:16.459
Meanwhile, Todd's right-hand woman Mrs. Nellie
Lovett portrayed by Burton's ex-wife and frequent

00:03:16.459 --> 00:03:20.940
collaborator Helena Bonham Carter uses his
"leftovers" as the main ingredient in her

00:03:20.940 --> 00:03:22.060
special meat pies.

00:03:22.400 --> 00:03:24.000
"What are we going to do about the boy, then?"

00:03:25.500 --> 00:03:26.540
"Send him up."

00:03:27.860 --> 00:03:29.760
"Oh, we don't need to worry about him — he's
a simple thing."

00:03:30.680 --> 00:03:35.920
The film slashed its way to the top of the
box office in December 2007, earning $152

00:03:35.939 --> 00:03:40.959
million worldwide against its $50 million
production budget, raking in dazzling reviews

00:03:40.960 --> 00:03:41.620
from critics.

00:03:41.960 --> 00:03:45.959
A National Board of Review-selected pick for
the top 10 movies of the year, Sweeney Todd

00:03:45.960 --> 00:03:50.599
also took home numerous Golden Globe Awards
and an Academy Award for Best Art Direction.

00:03:50.680 --> 00:03:55.040
Sweeney Todd leaves Netflix on September 1st,
so check it out now before it's too late.

00:03:55.280 --> 00:03:55.900
Chop chop!

00:03:56.780 --> 00:04:00.559
Eager for more Fast and Furious in your life
after catching the franchise spinoff Hobbs

00:04:00.560 --> 00:04:01.060
&amp; Shaw?

00:04:01.160 --> 00:04:05.019
Plan a back-to-back-to-back binge session
of three Fast and Furious films that won't

00:04:05.019 --> 00:04:07.319
be available to stream on Netflix for much
longer.

00:04:07.320 --> 00:04:09.590
They're going, going, GONE, baby.

00:04:09.860 --> 00:04:11.220
"Where's he going?"

00:04:12.100 --> 00:04:13.240
"Went to the carwash."

00:04:13.640 --> 00:04:15.299
"...go have him fetch my car."

00:04:16.040 --> 00:04:17.460
"Go fetch your car?"

00:04:17.960 --> 00:04:22.109
The first three entries in the high-octane
series are skidding away from Netflix on September

00:04:22.109 --> 00:04:27.340
1st: The Fast and the Furious, 2 Fast 2 Furious,
and The Fast and the Furious: Tokyo Drift.

00:04:27.340 --> 00:04:31.020
If you're looking for a mindless adrenaline
rush, you simply can't go wrong with this

00:04:31.020 --> 00:04:31.520
franchise.

00:04:31.780 --> 00:04:32.780
But you better get a move on...

00:04:38.920 --> 00:04:43.340
Adapted from Anthony Burgess's novel of the
same name, Stanley Kubrick's dark futuristic

00:04:43.340 --> 00:04:48.550
fantasy A Clockwork Orange follows the exploits
of a charismatic young sociopath named Alex,

00:04:48.550 --> 00:04:50.960
played with insidious glee by Malcolm McDowell.

00:04:51.240 --> 00:04:52.060
"Oh, jolly good."

00:04:52.520 --> 00:04:57.680
Alex and his merry band of thugs commit "ultra-violence"
wherever they go, until Alex is finally thrown

00:04:57.680 --> 00:05:00.319
in jail following one of his intensely heinous
crimes.

00:05:00.319 --> 00:05:04.900
In order to return to society, he agrees to
undergo rehabilitation through psychological

00:05:04.900 --> 00:05:05.460
conditioning.

00:05:05.660 --> 00:05:09.540
And when he's finally back on the streets,
it's Alex's turn to be the victim… or is

00:05:09.540 --> 00:05:10.120
it?

00:05:10.460 --> 00:05:14.080
Whether revisiting the film or checking it
out for the first time, you simply won't be

00:05:14.080 --> 00:05:15.620
able to take your eyes off the screen.

00:05:15.880 --> 00:05:19.720
Check out A Clockwork Orange before it leaves
Netflix on September 1st… because it would

00:05:19.720 --> 00:05:20.980
be a crime to miss it.

